    "q-120373": {
      "dom_id": "step-q120373",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A)=0.75,$ $P(B)=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{9}{10},$ find $P(A\\cap B).$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{9}{10} & =0.75+\\frac{1}{2}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.75+0.5-0.9 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo check our answer, we can construct the corresponding Venn diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/2be28c417aca14a91c8be4645af551c7b39d0ad9e8a467f01cef5092b531b383.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
