    "q-87118": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87118",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P(A\\cap B).$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+0.4-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.5+0.4-0.8 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo check our answer, we can construct the corresponding Venn diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/f3000baa7bbb8e8a181c1cfc848ecd0fd85e0d8509a1620bf478e10b10ff17d2.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
